# Wren, once the regalia is gathered and her own question is settled
# (TSC_WrenLay): the ending she has been waiting to stand at now has a
# place and a date. Fires as an initiation; foreshadows the sung answer
# to the Honor Guard.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_WrenBars

== start ==
Wren has the copied pages out again, flat on her knee, and she is not looking at them. She is looking east.

"I can almost hear it," she says. "The last four bars. Since the staff. Not the notes - the distilled essence of them."

* "The rider said you would know it when you got there." -> there
* "Almost?" -> there

== there ==
"When the fifth road ends, whoever is standing there will know how it goes." She says it like a lesson recited, and then, quieter: "The fifth road ends at that mound. We are carrying the end of it in our saddlebags."

She rolls the pages and puts them away, in the lute case, next to the strings, where they have been since the monastery.

"Eight hundred years of unfinished. When we go down that stair, keep me alive and near the front. I have a delivery to make, and I am going to make it *well*."

* "Near the front. Done." -> end
    do grant_xp(40); affinity(+5)
